WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.868
-I'm here with
Scarlett Johansson right there!

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:06.400
It's like
a show from the future.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.601
This is so wild.

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.801
We're about to play
"The Mimic Challenge."

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:10.968
Here we go.

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:13.100
-♪ Mimic Challenge ♪

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.334
♪ Mimic, Mimic Challenge,
yeah ♪

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.200
All right, bud.
Here's how it works.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.133
We're gonna take turns making
noises with different objects,

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:23.968
and the other person
has to immediately

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:28.667
match that sound as precisely
as they can into the microphone.

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:31.400
-Now, how do you know --
how do you know if you won?

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.267
Like, what's the --
-Audience response?

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.501
-Okay, fair enough.
You're right.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:36.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.000
-Since you're my guest,
you're gonna make

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.934
the first noise,
and I will mimic your noise.

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.367
-Okay.
I have all these props

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:46.467
over here,
so this is the first one.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.400
-Okay.
-I've never done these.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.801
I don't know
what kind of noises these make.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.200
-I don't even know what that is.
-Bear with me.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:54.734
What does it look like?

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.434
♪♪

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.400
-Uh...
A thermometer?

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.801
-It's a thermometer.
Okay.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:09.534
[ Plastic crinkling ]

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:12.000
Erh! Erh!
Errrrrr!

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.400
Errrrr-rr-rr-rr!

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.400
All right.
That was okay.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.033
Thank you.
Now, oh, here we go.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:23.601
This is good.
Now it's your turn to mimic.

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:26.200
-Oh, no.
-Okay. Ready?

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.734
[ Lettuce crunching ]

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:33.100
-I'm supposed to make
that sound with my voice?

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.968
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:36.968
Yep.

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.200
-Ch-cha-koo-tuh!

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:41.367
Ckk-ckk-ckk!

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.968
-Oh, my God!
Nailed it!

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.234
[ Ding! ]
[ Laughs ]

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.968
You nailed it!
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.467
-It's uncanny.
-No, it's so good.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:55.100
Okay.
-All right, I got this.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.167
-Ooh, I like that guy.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.100
-"Squeeze the Jabber Ball."

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.367
[ Jabber Ball squeak ]

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:03.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.267
-Okay.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.133
Rrr-eeee-uh.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:09.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Ding! ]

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.868
-Not bad?
Wow.

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:13.834
I'm actually
the voice of that doll.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.501
For years, yeah.
Okay.

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:21.434
Oh, this one is --
It's a very odd thing.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.667
An otamatone,
this thing is called.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:24.968
All right,
let me show you what it does.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:28.267
You press the sides, and its
mouth opens a little bit.

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:31.901
[ High-pitched squeaking ]

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:33.601
-Ee-eeeeeeeee!

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.534
-[ Laughs ]
[ Ding! ]

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:38.434
All right.
You have another career.

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:39.934
You have a whole nother career
in doing this.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.667
-Ee-eeeeeeeee!

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:43.000
-Oh, my God.
-Is that better?

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.601
-Yeah, I feel like
all these dogs

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:47.200
are just gonna start
running to the studio.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.567
Ee-eeeee!
All right.

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.701
-Is that right?
Whoa!

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:54.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.367
-Wow! It gets bigger.
Oh, my God.

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.901
That's a --
That's a vuvuzela.

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:01.934
-Excusez-moi?
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:03.400
[ Laughter ]
This is fantastic.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.234
I love these things.
They were banned at, like,

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:07.667
all these football games,
soccer games,

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:09.868
'cause they were too annoying.

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:13.434
-And we're about
to find out why.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:18.934
[ Vuvuzela blowing ]

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.234
-Oh, gosh.
-Is that right?

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.734
-All right, let me try.

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:26.334
Pbbbbht!
Pffbbbbhhht!

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:28.467
[ Ding! ]
Pfffbbbbbbbbhhht!

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:32.067
-Whoa!
-Pfffbbbbbbbbhhht!

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.467
Pfffbbbbbbbbhhht!

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:35.934
-Very nice.
-All right, Scarlett,

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:36.901
I think you're
gonna do this one.

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:40.734
This one's gonna be good.

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:45.834
[ Whipped cream spraying ]

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:48.601
-Cwwwkkkkk!

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:51.634
-Whoa! I thought
that was really happening!

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:53.834
That one's actually amazing.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:56.467
I thought I was still putting
the whipped cream out.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:57.901
Fantastic.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:00.133
-I'm saving that
for after the show, yeah.

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:02.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:05.167
-To put it on ice cream?
-[ Chuckles ] Sure.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:11.767
[ Noisemaker cranking ]

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:15.100
-Uh-h-h-h-h-h-h-h-h!

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:19.267
[ Applause ]
[ Ding! ]

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:23.100
[ Noisemaker slowly cranking ]
Uh-h-h-h-h-h-h-h.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:29.234
It's like, a-a-a-all right,
all right, all right.

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:30.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:33.834
All right, last one here.
All right. Ready?

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:35.000
All right, here --
it's a little...

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.000
[ Porcupine toy chittering ]

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.868
-Wee-ee-ee, boo-wee-ee-ee!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:46.868
-Wow. That's how a professional
does it right there.

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:49.033
My thanks to Scarlett Johansson!

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:52.601
"Sing 2" is in theaters
everywhere December 22nd.

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:54.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
2-2-2.

